WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.706
Articulate 360 is best understood as an eLearning authoring ecosystem rather than a single magic button for training.

2
00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:18.417
It brings together tools for building courses, creating interactions, managing review, using media assets, and publishing learning content for online delivery.

3
00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:29.514
In a practical training team, that means one environment may support slide-based courses, responsive lessons, assessments, stakeholder review, and LMS-ready output.

4
00:00:29.514 --> 00:00:32.596
It helps to separate the parts of the ecosystem.

5
00:00:32.596 --> 00:00:36.449
Authoring tools are where the course is designed and built.

6
00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:40.302
Review tools support comments, approvals, and revisions.

7
00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:46.929
Media assets provide starting points for visuals, icons, templates, and character-style elements.

8
00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:56.716
Publishing formats control how the course is delivered, while the learning platform or LMS handles launch, tracking, reporting, and learner access.

9
00:00:56.716 --> 00:01:08.352
Common use cases include compliance training, technical training, onboarding, microlearning, software training, product education, and scenario-based decision practice.

10
00:01:08.352 --> 00:01:11.974
These courses may look very different from one another.

11
00:01:11.974 --> 00:01:17.368
A short policy refresher might need a clean responsive structure and a simple quiz.

12
00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:21.837
A software workflow course might need demonstrations and practice.

13
00:01:21.837 --> 00:01:26.307
A leadership scenario might need branching decisions and feedback.

14
00:01:26.307 --> 00:01:29.466
The tool does not replace instructional design.

15
00:01:29.466 --> 00:01:36.479
Strong courses begin with a reason for learning, a learner audience, a performance gap, and a clear outcome.

16
00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:40.871
Features matter, but features without purpose can create clutter.

17
00:01:40.871 --> 00:01:48.962
The best Articulate 360 projects use the tool to support learning, not to show off every interaction or animation available.

18
00:01:48.962 --> 00:01:55.666
A useful way to frame Articulate 360 work is to treat each project as a learning product with a lifecycle.

19
00:01:55.666 --> 00:02:03.912
It begins with a need, moves through design and development, passes through review and testing, and eventually needs updates.

20
00:02:03.912 --> 00:02:13.544
Thinking in lifecycle terms keeps the team from focusing only on the initial build and forgetting maintainability, tracking, and learner support.
